  "oral_argument": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-463a78cada97-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, chief Justice Roberts: We will hear argument, we'll continue argument, in Case 22-535, Department of Education versus Brown. Welcome back."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-463a78cada97-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Thomas, justice Thomas: Are there any instances in which you would have procedural standing?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-463a78cada97-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 7,
              "start": 7
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, justice Sotomayor: The -- this action has nothing to do with their right if they thought it was permissible to seek relief under the Education Act, correct?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-463a78cada97-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 25,
              "start": 25
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Chief Justice Roberts: Counsel, I'm -- I'm sure I'm misreading the graphs on -- I'm looking at 247, 248. Didn't half the borrowers say they would not have any trouble paying their loans without regard to the forgiveness program?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-463a78cada97-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 35,
              "start": 35
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, justice Alito: Why is it fair?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-463a78cada97-0001-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 37,
              "start": 37
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, justice Sotomayor: I take your bottom\u2011line answer to be everybody suffered in the pandemic, but different people got different benefits because they qualified under different programs, correct?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-463a78cada97-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kagan, justice Kagan: I mean, Congress passed a statute that dealt with loan repayment for colleges, and it didn't pass a statute that dealt with loan repayment for lawn businesses."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-463a78cada97-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 48,
              "start": 48
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kavanaugh, justice Kavanaugh: If --if it were party\u2011specific relief and it went up to the court of appeals and the court of -- and you had sought an emergency injunction in the court of appeals and the court of appeals ruled against the government on that, would you then follow that in that circuit or not?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-463a78cada97-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 57,
              "start": 57
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Thomas, justice Thomas: Mr. Connolly, has this Court ever held that the notice\u2011and\u2011comment provisions of the APA can establish \u2014 are enough for standing in a \u2014 in a case like this?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-463a78cada97-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 60,
              "start": 60
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, justice Sotomayor: Except my biggest problem is you've shown me nothing to suggest that if they'd have to or will go under HEA, that they're going to deprive you of due process."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-463a78cada97-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 66,
              "start": 66
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kagan, justice Kagan: But, Mr. Connolly, aren't you really fighting Congress on this one?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-463a78cada97-0003-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 67,
              "start": 67
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Barrett, justice Barrett: Mr. Connolly, what are the limits of your theory?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "463a78cada97e3c67158872692ba4c6999b4de384652196f4e344e465231d480",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-463a78cada97-0003-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 72,
              "start": 72
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kavanaugh, justice Kavanaugh: So, for purposes of standing, as distinct as to who can comment, because anyone can comment \u2014"
      }
    ],
